# God's Eye View — Docker deployment environment.
# Copy to .env and fill in. This file is a REFERENCE: no real keys or hosts.
#
# Container notes (differs from .env.example):
#   * Configuration is read at container START. There is no in-app Provider
#     Settings panel in a container — it is dev-server-only and refuses
#     proxied requests by design.
#   * The app has NO authentication of its own. It brokers spendable API
#     keys. Put it behind your reverse proxy + identity provider and set
#     provider-side budget caps (OpenAI usage limits, Google Cloud budgets)
#     as the real spend backstop. The built-in per-IP rate limiters are NOT
#     billing caps and key on the proxy's IP when behind a reverse proxy.
#   * Run a SINGLE replica. Rate limits, the AISStream connection, HLS
#     session caps, the TomTom daily tile budget, and the .gev-cache writers
#     all assume one process.
#   * The working directory holds runtime caches (.gev-cache/, .gev-logs/)
#     in anonymous volumes; do not mount the repo root read-only over them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED for any non-localhost deployment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The exact public hostname(s) this instance is served on, comma-separated.
# The app blocks any request whose Host header is not in this allowlist
# (DNS-rebinding defense). Exact names only — wildcard/leading-dot entries
# are silently dropped. Must match the Host your reverse proxy forwards.
# GEV_ALLOWED_HOSTS=globe.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment / proxy plumbing (compose.yaml reads these)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Traefik docker network, entrypoint, cert resolver, and forward-auth
# middleware. Adjust to your proxy.
# GEV_PROXY_NETWORK=proxy
# GEV_PROXY_ENTRYPOINT=websecure
# GEV_CERT_RESOLVER=letsencrypt
# GEV_AUTH_MIDDLEWARE=authentik-forward-auth

# Public hostname for the app (used in the Traefik router rule).
# GEV_APP_HOSTNAME=globe.example.com

# Optional MCP sidecar port (app profile only).
# GEV_MCP_PORT=4174

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App behavior
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=4173

# Optional: tighten the per-IP rate limits for the cost-bearing endpoints
# (in requests per minute). Defaults are 30 (OpenAI) and 120 (Google Places).
# Behind a reverse proxy these key on the proxy address, so treat them as a
# per-deployment throttle, not per-user.
# GEV_RATELIMIT_OPENAI_PER_MIN=30
# GEV_RATELIMIT_GOOGLE_PER_MIN=120

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-exposed keys (baked into the bundle AT BUILD TIME)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These three are compiled into the static bundle and are visible in browser
# devtools by design. Scope/restrict them at the provider for your deployment
# origin (Google: HTTP referrer + API restrictions; Cesium: public
# assets:read token with URL restrictions). Rotating one requires a rebuild.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=
# MAPILLARY_CLIENT_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side keys (read at RUNTIME from the container environment)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app starts without any of these — layers that need a key simply show
# as key-required or fall back (traffic runs a built-in simulation without
# TomTom). Add what you want live.

# OpenAI Realtime voice control.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_REALTIME_MODEL=gpt-realtime-2
# OPENAI_REALTIME_MODEL_MINI=gpt-realtime-2.1-mini
# OPENAI_REALTIME_VOICE=marin
# OPENAI_REALTIME_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# OPENAI_HUD_SUMMARY_MODEL=gpt-5-nano
# OPENAI_REALTIME_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-transcribe

# Google server-side calls (Places / Street View fallback). Falls back to
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY when unset.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_SERVER_API_KEY=

# NASA FIRMS active fires (free key: https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/)
# FIRMS_MAP_KEY=

# AISStream vessels (https://aisstream.io/)
# AISSTREAM_API_KEY=
# VITE_AIS_LIVE_MAX_ROWS=12000
# VITE_AIS_LIVE_LABEL_MAX_ROWS=900
# AISSTREAM_SILENCE_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# OpenSky aircraft. Default mode is oauth (needs client credentials); "anon"
# works but is rate-limited.
OPENSKY_AUTH_MODE=anon
# OPENSKY_CLIENT_ID=
# OPENSKY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# TomTom traffic (free tier: 200K tile requests/month).
# TOMTOM_API_KEY=
# TOMTOM_DAILY_TILE_BUDGET=6000

# Launch Library 2 (optional, public access works without a token).
# LL2_API_TOKEN=

# Local ADS-B receiver feeds (dump1090/readsb aircraft.json over HTTP).
# URLs must be loopback, RFC1918, localhost, or *.local FROM THE CONTAINER's
# network namespace — a bare "localhost" here means the container itself.
# LOCAL_RECEIVER_FEEDS=

# Overpass: comma-separated instances; use only ones you run or pay for.
# OVERPASS_UPSTREAMS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not applicable / dead in a container — do not bother
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The in-app Provider Settings panel (/api/setup/*) is dev-server-only and
# refuses proxied requests; supply keys via this file / container env.
# ChatGPT-OAuth voice sign-in spawns a desktop browser; use OPENAI_API_KEY.
# The /mcp HTTP endpoint is loopback-only; use the compose "mcp" profile.
